For many years, I believed that was the way to train pets. Recently
I was mucking around in wizmode and noticed that you can observe the
pet's aport (right name?) with a stethoscope. As I was playing a healer,
I knew the stone to flesh spell, so I converted some rocks to meatballs
and fed the pet until his aport was 20 (max?). He then proceeded to 
empty the store in nothing flat. Try this as a healer and you can 
quickly empty a store at a cost of four or five meatballs. Note that
aport is reduced by 1 each time your pet drops something in front of
you, so an occasional treat for reenforcement is a good idea.

Now I prereward my pet as soon as I've rearranged the store, putting the
stuff I want individually close to the door and everything else in a far
courner. Seems to work a little faster to me. YMMV.
 
